On 31 March, the cash book of Ebere Ventures showed a debit bank balance of N236,400, while the bank statement on the same date showed a credit balance of N265,800. A comparison revealed:
(i) cheques issued but not yet presented: N48,000 and N22,500;
(ii) a deposit of N35,000 made on 31 March had not been credited by the bank;
(iii) bank charges of N2,600 appeared only on the bank statement;
(iv) a dividend of N18,000 was received directly by the bank;
(v) a standing order for insurance, N12,500, was paid by the bank;
(vi) a customer's cheque for N9,000 was dishonoured.
(a) Prepare the adjusted cash book (bank columns). [10 marks]
(b) Prepare a bank reconciliation statement starting with the adjusted cash book balance. [10 marks]
